Subject: [SE3-P3] qasf: flush every stream when seeking

The WM ASF Reader's seek (IMediaSeeking::ChangeCurrent) flushes downstream
before stopping the asynchronous reader, but both loops flushed the seeked
stream's peer stream_count times and never flushed the other streams. With
an audio and a video stream, the reader's callback thread can be blocked
delivering a sample to the unflushed renderer, and the same thread has to
process the stop, so WMT_STOPPED never arrives and the seek hangs
(intermittently, depending on which stream was being delivered). Flush the
peer of every connected stream, as GE's ge-video-rework 0027 already makes
graph Stop release blocked deliveries.

---
diff --git a/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c b/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
--- a/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
+++ b/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
@@ -404,10 +404,14 @@
 
     TRACE("iface %p.\n", iface);
 
-    /* Send begin flush commands downstream. */
+    /* Send begin flush commands downstream. Every stream must be flushed: the
+     * reader's callback thread can be blocked delivering to any of them, and it
+     * also has to process the stop. */
     for (i = 0; i < filter->stream_count; ++i)
     {
-        if (FAILED(IPin_BeginFlush(stream->source.pin.peer)))
+        IPin *peer = filter->streams[i].source.pin.peer;
+
+        if (peer && FAILED(IPin_BeginFlush(peer)))
             WARN("Failed to BeginFlush for stream %u.\n", i);
     }
 
@@ -417,7 +421,9 @@
     /* Send end flush commands downstream. */
     for (i = 0; i < filter->stream_count; ++i)
     {
-        if (FAILED(IPin_EndFlush(stream->source.pin.peer)))
+        IPin *peer = filter->streams[i].source.pin.peer;
+
+        if (peer && FAILED(IPin_EndFlush(peer)))
             WARN("Failed to EndFlush for stream %u.\n", i);
     }
 
